{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (rebar-debug Phase 1 — confirmed at runtime)\n\n**Mechanism.** pytest's default `prepend` import mode inserts a collected module's *basedir*\n(its first ancestor without `__init__.py`) at `sys.path[0]`. `tests/unit/` has no\n`__init__.py`, so collecting ANY `tests/unit/**` module puts `tests/unit` at `sys.path[0]`.\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/__init__.py` (empty, 0 bytes) then makes that directory an\nimportable top-level package named `rebar_reconciler`, **shadowing** the engine package that\n`tests/scripts/conftest.py:28-30` puts on `sys.path` further down.\n\n`tests/scripts/reducer/test_managed_refs.py:42-48` exec's `outbound_differ.py` standalone via\n`spec_from_file_location` with no package context, so its module-level\n`from rebar_reconciler._loader import lazy_load` (`outbound_differ.py:31`) resolves\n`rebar_reconciler` through ordinary top-level machinery — and gets the empty test-dir package,\nwhich has no `_loader` submodule.\n\nThe repo already has a compensating mechanism for exactly this shadow:\n`_seed_dotted_namespace()` in `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conftest.py:51-79` appends the engine\n`rebar_reconciler` directory to the shadow package's `__path__` so \"ANY engine submodule falls\nthrough generically\" (its own comment). It was added by f32b19b1e7.\n\n**The defect is that the compensation is installed one directory too deep.** It lives in\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conftest.py`, so it fires only when `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/**`\nis collected — but the shadow it compensates for is created by ANY `tests/unit/**` collection.\n\n**Discriminating evidence.** I instrumented the failing fixture to print\n`rebar_reconciler.__file__` / `__path__` / `sys.path[:6]` at the moment `outbound_differ` is\nexec'd. Three runs, one varying input (which `tests/unit` modules are in the selection):\n\n| selection | `rebar_reconciler.__file__` | `__path__` | result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| the reducer test alone | `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__init__.py` | `[engine pkg]` | PASS |\n| `+ tests/unit/test_epoch_guard_matrix.py` | `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/__init__.py` | `['tests/unit/rebar_reconciler']` | **ERROR (reported)** |\n| `+ tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_lock_steal.py` | `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/__init__.py` | `['tests/unit/rebar_reconciler', 'src/.../rebar_reconciler']` | PASS |\n\nIn the failing run `sys.path[0]` was `tests/unit` with the engine dir at index 3. Row 3 is the\ndecisive one: the shadow is *present and harmless* once the `__path__` extension has run, which\nrules out the rival explanations — it is not a `sys.path` ordering race per se, not a stale\n`__pycache__`, not a `sys.modules` pin (no seeded key was involved), and not an installed\nsite-packages copy (none exists in the venv).\n\n**Why the full suite is green.** Conftests import at *collection* time for the whole arg set, so\na run that includes `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/**` always fires the compensation. The bug is\nreachable only when `tests/unit/**` is collected WITHOUT `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/**` — which\npytest-randomly's varying selections and any developer's partial selection produce.\n\n**The compensation is already duplicated, which corroborates the scoping defect.** Two further\ncopies exist, both in `tests/unit/` top level, each with a comment pointing back at the conftest:\n`tests/unit/test_canonical_consolidation.py:59-71` and\n`tests/unit/test_code_review_artifact.py:110-118`. Two prior authors hit this same shadow from a\ntop-level `tests/unit` module and patched locally rather than hoisting.\n\n**Legitimacy: `defect`.** An existing test errors, and the behaviour violates the cited design\ninvariant of `_seed_dotted_namespace()` itself — that engine submodules resolve generically under\nthe shadow.\n\n**Repair is mechanical (verified, not asserted).** An independent adversarial pass measured the\nalternatives and eliminated them on evidence, leaving one: hoist the `__path__` extension to\n`tests/unit/conftest.py`.\n- deleting `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/__init__.py` -> 10 collection errors (23 files there use\n  relative imports), plus 8 sub-packages would become generically-named top-level packages;\n- `--import-mode=importlib` -> 9512 collected / 23 errors vs. a clean 11198 / 0 baseline;\n- renaming the directory -> 290 tracked files, 53 references across 30 files, and it discards the\n  deliberate `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/` mirroring;\n- changing the engine -> bends production code (194 dotted imports across 54 modules) to a test\n  directory's name.\n\n**One trap recorded for the implementer:** placing the hoist *after*\n`tests/unit/conftest.py:21-22` is WRONG. By then the engine dir is `sys.path[0]`, so\n`import rebar_reconciler` permanently binds the ENGINE package before pytest creates the shadow;\n`__path__.append` becomes a no-op and `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` then dies with\n`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'rebar_reconciler.conftest'`. It looks green on the\nticket's repro and is red one command over. The extension must resolve the shadow while\n`tests/unit` is still `sys.path[0]` (or seed it explicitly).\n\n**Guard shape.** An in-process assertion would be masked in CI — a full-suite run always collects\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/**`, so the invariant holds even with the fix reverted (measured: the\nnaive guard passes when run alongside `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_lock_steal.py`). The guard\nmust therefore be a subprocess, matching the precedent already in\n`tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py::test_library_path_exposes_no_generic_top_level_engine_names`,\nwhose docstring cites the same masking hazard."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786101981852415001,"uuid":"9d988fa8-0624-4e27-a668-4398877df966"}